  "summary": "Malicious code in dolyame-boxy-independent-bnpl-text-block (npm)",
  "details": "On require, the package downloads a platform-specific binary payload from Cloudflare Workers endpoints (oob-worker[.]cf102-baf[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf100-416[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf103-070[.]workers[.]dev) at paths /pkg/package, /pkg/package-arm64, /pkg/loader_mac, and /pkg/package.exe, with a DNS TXT-record fallback channel via c[.]sdk[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru. It writes the downloaded payload to /var/tmp/.cache_\u003chex\u003e (or dotnet_diag_\u003chex\u003e.exe in TEMP on Windows), marks it executable, and launches it as a detached background process. A stamp file at /tmp/.analytics_state throttles re-downloads. The package otherwise exposes a stub \"text block\" class and serves no legitimate function.",
